Actually, this appears to be a benchmark/swe-bench style task. The real httpx issue about RFC 2069 mode digest auth. Let me recall what the fix was.

RFC 2069 is the older digest auth spec where `qop` is not present in the challenge. In RFC 2069, the response is computed as:

```
HA1 = MD5(username:realm:password)
HA2 = MD5(method:digestURI)
response = MD5(HA1:nonce:HA2)
```

Without qop. RFC 2617 adds qop support:
```
HA1 = MD5(username:realm:password)
HA2 = MD5(method:digestURI)
response = MD5(HA1:nonce:nc:cnonce:qop:HA2)
```

The issue in httpx: when qop is absent (RFC 2069 mode), the code still includes qop-related fields, producing an incorrect response.

